From aeccf91a33d6f8431bb014fb2f53e38e72c9809b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stew Forster <stew675@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 06:50:35 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 13/14] rdna-boosts: block 13: fused MoE gate+up+GLU MMQ + mmvq
 short-K item-split

- fused MoE gate+up+GLU MMQ (prefill) on RDNA4, gated to the instantiated
  type list (Q3_K/Q4_K/Q5_K/Q8_0/Q6_K)
- mmvq short-K decode item-split re-based on the upstream has_fusion mmvq path
- multi-token mmvq x_scale_channel_dst fusion: extend the MoE down x topk-weights
  MUL fold from single-token (n=1) to MUL_MAT_ID batches (spec-dec verify
  n=2..8); mul_mat_vec_q_moe applies x_scale[channel_dst + token_idx*nchannels_dst]
- fix ROCm unaligned-width split-load (Q6_K/Q3_K 2-GPU): set_tensor_2d stages
  via aligned H2D + unaligned D2D, byte-identical
- test-backend-ops: extend the qwen35moe-family MUL_MAT_ID_FUSION sweep with
  the fused types (bs 1/4/512); 16222/16222 pass

- REGRESSION FIX (2026-09-04): the block-13 mmvq item-split kernel + RDNA
  rows_per_block override collapsed multi-token decode batches (ncols 2..8,
  the speculative/MTP verify step): its per-thread accumulator fan-out
  tmp[ncols_dst][rpb] (4 tokens x rpb<=16) is register-bound, and the rpb=16
  override also lost ~4% on long-K (K>=4096) single-token decode. Fix: re-add
  the pre-block-13 K-split kernel as mul_mat_vec_q_ksplit and dispatch decode
  batches ncols 2..8 to it (dense and MoE plain rows); at ncols==1, rows with
  K >= 4096 (dense qkv/FFN projections, any quant type) also use ksplit while
  short-K MoE rows (K < 4096) keep the item-split/rpb path. Verified
  (1x R9700 gfx1201): dense qwen35 27B Q4_K_XL adaptive-MTP 18.3 -> 27.5 t/s
  (bit-identical to the 12-block build), plain decode 29.0 -> 30.1 (+3.1-3.7%
  at d0/d16384/d65536); qwen35moe A3B adaptive-MTP 36.3 -> 55.8 t/s with
  single-token decode unchanged (Q6_K tg128 98.3 vs 97.59 recorded baseline).

- REGRESSION FIX (2026-09-02, folded into block 13): MoE MTP verify-numerics
  collapse. The rms_norm->mmvq Q8_1 quantize-cache fold (block 08) corrupts
  multi-token MUL_MAT_ID; the fold is gated to single-token MMID + plain
  MUL_MAT consumers (acceptance 0 -> 0.51, draft-mtp 53 -> 126 t/s).

- Amended 2026-09-05 with the RDNA3_5 (Strix Halo, gfx1151) and RDNA3_0
  (gfx1100) fused-MoE-MMQ gate relaxations - see patches/README.md block-13
  notes and the dated benchmark records.

- Amended 2026-09-06 with the model-neutral Strix MoE mmq folds (routed mmq,
  swiglu-input quantize, mwr float4, split_j/Q8_0 rows, quantize chunk,
  mul_mat_q_pair, weighted-down mmvq, scale-unary window) - see
  patches/README.md and wip/archive/qwen4exp/README.md.
